    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1997-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Listing out all the two-digit multiples of \\(7,\\) we get \\[ 14, 21, 28, 35, 42, 49, 56, 63, 70,\\] \\[ 77, 84, 91, 98. \\] We have that \\(28\\) and \\(91\\) are the two multiples whose digits add to \\(10.\\)\n\nThe sum of these numbers is \\(28 + 91 = 119.\\)\n\nThus, A is the correct answer.",
